+
+### Optional ICMP traffic variation
+
+`padding_max` (`-padding-max`) accepts 0..64, default 0. The capacity examples use 32. Padding is authenticated and encrypted, with 3 bytes of framing plus 0..N bytes per request, mirrored in its Echo Reply. Existing protobuf peers accept it. Echo-mode heartbeat timing varies by ±10%; application data is not deliberately delayed. This does not conceal ICMP or guarantee DPI resistance. See [deployment and limitations](ICMP-RELEASE.fa.md).
